  "method": {
    "discretisation": "Existing P1 cell/face velocity and pressure, P2 potential, Laplacian Stokes, ordinary cell L2 force, B/-B^T, unchanged geometry and Solver gate. Only analytic fixture and native boundary residual output added.",
    "reference_scales": "Lref=1 m,Uref=1 m/s,nu=1 m^2/s,density-normalised pressure. xi=x/Lref-s*y/Lref,eta=y/Lref; s=0 or0.7.",
    "analytic_solution": "g(t)=t^2(1-t)^2; psi=64*Uref*Lref*g(xi)*g(eta); u=(partial_y psi,-partial_x psi),p=Uref^2*sin(pi*xi)*sin(pi*eta); f=-nu*Laplacian(u)+grad(p).",
    "boundary": "All four physical walls are stationary, exact velocity prescribed identically zero for both face modes. g and its first derivative vanish at both ends. Wrong square/shear geometry pairing explicitly rejected.",
    "traction": "For each boundary face and velocity component, moments are the assembled local stiffness row times u minus B^T row times gauge-corrected pressure. Includes stabilisation. Reconstruct P1 traction as (r0+12*s_face*r1)/face_length. It is the native conservative variational traction, not a raw velocity-gradient trace.",
    "traction_reference": "Physical sigma*n=[nu*(grad(u)+grad(u)^T)-p*I]*n. For the analytic divergence-free stationary no-slip solution, transpose-gradient traction vanishes, so physical and Laplacian tractions agree. Does not assert equivalence for general moving boundaries or nonzero discrete divergence.",
    "momentum_balance": "Norm of sum over all outer-face reaction integrals plus integral over all cells of f; every wall and cell included. No new acceptance tolerance.",
    "units": "velocity RMS and wall velocity m/s; pressure and traction RMS m^2/s^2; integrated 2D momentum balance m^3/s^2; divergence s^-1; pressure work m^4/s^3; sampled maxima only, not continuous maxima.",
    "cost_scope": "10 native small solves, including assembly and field output; no claim of full-flow or exclusive-machine speedup."
  },
